A Cloud Center of Excellence (CCoE) is a cross-functional team that helps an organization establish and improve its cloud adoption practices.

A CCoE may include specialists from:

* Cloud architecture
* Security
* Networking
* Infrastructure
* Finance
* Compliance
* DevOps
* Application development

Its responsibilities can include creating standards, reviewing architectures, developing reusable patterns, educating teams, and promoting cost-effective cloud adoption.

For example, a CCoE can create a standardized Azure landing zone that application teams use when onboarding new workloads.

A real-life use case is a large organization transitioning from traditional datacenter infrastructure to Azure and needing centralized expertise to guide multiple teams.

A CCoE accelerates cloud adoption while maintaining consistency and governance.
